{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Vantaa ja Kerava lags nationally in crude life-prolonging treatment at 20.3% (95% CI 17.3–23.8) versus 30.4% and crude recorded MDT meetings at 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9) versus 6.0%.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:life_prolonging:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:life_prolonging",
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "In Vantaa ja Kerava, the crude life-prolonging treatment share is 20.3% (95% CI 17.3–23.8; n=121/595), where the 95% confidence interval excludes the national value of 30.4% (4522/14873), while the crude curative treatment share of 35.6% (95% CI 31.9–39.6; n=212/595) has a 95% confidence interval that excludes the national 27.0% (4009/14873) upward.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:curative:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The crude symptomatic treatment share is 36.1% (95% CI 32.4–40.1; n=215/595) versus 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally, and the crude share with no treatment record within 12 months—mixing untreated patients and unrecorded treatment—is 28.9% (95% CI 25.4–32.7; n=172/595) versus 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally, with each 95% confidence interval including the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:symptomatic:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The crude share of patients with a recorded MDT meeting is 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9; n=1/595), whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national value of 6.0% (893/14873), though this measures HILMO recording from direct patient contacts rather than actual multidisciplinary care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Nationally, preliminary unpublished figures show lung cancer takes 155 days on average from symptoms to treatment in Finland (56 days patient delay, 41 days primary care, and 58 days specialist care) versus 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark, though public data do not measure county wait times.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist",
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "County treatment figures are crude and unadjusted for stage, while public registry data do not capture primary care, referrals, or treatment wait times.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
        "bs:coverage:Referral",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "All county treatment shares are crude—unadjusted for age or stage because stage at diagnosis is missing for ~48% of new patients—and treatment categories overlap, while Kuva 16 provides only digitised national age-adjusted curative reference lines of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women (±0.5 percentage points).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Reading the crude 28.9% (95% CI 25.4–32.7) no-treatment-record share as a data-quality signal is an inference, not a finding: since 28.9% is above the 27.5% national value (though its 95% confidence interval includes 27.5%), the low crude 20.3% (95% CI 17.3–23.8) life-prolonging share versus 30.4% nationally may partly reflect unrecorded treatment.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article found HILMO diagnoses matched the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, but that concerns diagnosis concordance only and says nothing about how completely treatment, referrals, or MDT meetings are recorded.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "q:950a2f797b"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure symptom onset, referrals, imaging waits, or county wait times for specialist visits and treatment start, while primary care visits are not included in the report's data and occupational health is not mentioned at all.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends auditing stage, drug, and MDT recording completeness, tracking access times using THL 21/2016 definitions, and standardising referrals and diagnostic coordination.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:3",
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Given Vantaa ja Kerava's crude 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9) recorded MDT share, crude 20.3% (95% CI 17.3–23.8) life-prolonging share, and crude 28.9% (95% CI 25.4–32.7) no-treatment-record share, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding while a national quality registry with 90% coverage including stage is planned.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Vantaan_ja_Keravan_hyvinvointialue",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:4c7a01d84c",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion and Finland lacks a unified pathway monitoring system, the team recommends reporting referral-to-treatment access times and flagging stalled handovers using THL guidance 21/2016 definitions for 16 cancers.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "q:4e702a20fe",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:24169121a4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While the roadmap plans national pathways, referral criteria, and coordinator guidance by 2026–2028 (for county adoption by 2029–2031) and the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation is due before the 2030 mid-term evaluation, the team recommends a standard referral template, a persistent-symptoms referral rule, and a diagnostic contact person, since mentor insight notes weak referrals get lower urgency ratings.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "q:556431a0c2"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
